Chapter: CdxCheckout
  cites Works chapter RepoProtocolPersist
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts
  cites Kernel chapter AppPersist
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The read half of the real repository tools: it opens the fact store on the
 attached disk, rebuilds the index by replaying the log, walks the tree, and
 prints the current version of every path -- the source, exactly as it was
 stored, checked out of a block device with no Perforce in the chain. Paired
 with cdx-store it is a round trip: a file goes in through one and comes back
 out through the other.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Device.Block, Console] Nothing = act
    let ix = repo-index-from-disk disk-load
    in print-uni (repo-checkout ix)
  end

